# 基本図形編集のプロセスで文字枠を編集する (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py: a figure of
# 30 small rectangles, two zigzag lines and one piece of text "ABC" (mkbig fig 30 4 1; its box
# from 100,120 to 220,160 of the figure, 210,247 to 330,287 on the screen). The same is done
# with the desktop's figure editor and with the one running as a process: the text pressed
# twice to edit it, the caret put at the head of its line, the letter after it deleted, the
# caret put at the end, letters typed in 英語 (in the width the input mode says), かな typed
# after ひらがなカタカナ and committed with Enter, 英数 back to 英語, the paragraph broken,
# Escape to end it, the figure saved. Record 0 comes out the same, byte for byte.
# Keys: Home 4A, Delete 4C, End 4D, Enter 28, Esc 29, ひらがなカタカナ 88, 英数 39;
# with Ctrl (01) S 16, E 08.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 30 4 1
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
dclick 215 255
sync 600
key 4A
key 4C
key 4D
text xy
key 88
text kana
sync 600
shot text_kernel_kana
key 28
key 39
key 28
sync 600
shot text_kernel_typing
key 29
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
shot text_kernel
sum show
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 30 4 1
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 33
wait 500
logmark
dclick 215 255
expectsince figure: text editing begun
key 4A
key 4C
key 4D
text xy
key 88
text kana
wait 300
shot text_process_kana
key 28
key 39
key 28
wait 300
shot text_process_typing
logmark
key 29
expectsince figure: text editing ended
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
shot text_process
sum show
same kernel
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
